{"version":"1","source":"Architectural Atlas procedural model","scope":"Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests, Beijing (simple)","title":"Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests","location":"Beijing, China","blurb":"The Temple of Heaven’s great circular hall in simplified schematic form: a 38 m triple-eaved timber hall without nails on a three-tiered marble terrace.","sourceUrls":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Temple of Heaven","url":"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Heaven"}],"systems":[{"id":"marble-terraces","name":"Marble terraces","color":"#e8e4da","description":"The three-tiered marble terrace, 6 m high, with its white marble balustrades and stairs."},{"id":"pillars","name":"Pillars","color":"#a83a2a","description":"The 28 wooden pillars: 4 Dragon Well (seasons), 12 gold (months), 12 eave (watches)."},{"id":"dougong-brackets","name":"Dougong brackets","color":"#8a4a30","description":"The layered interlocking bracket rings, assembled without nails."},{"id":"walls-doors","name":"Walls","color":"#7a5a3a","description":"The circular timber wall panels. Arrangement is schematic."},{"id":"roofs","name":"Roofs and finial","color":"#2e4a7a","description":"The triple blue-tiled eaves, fascia rings, spouts and the gilded baoding knob."},{"id":"dome-interior","name":"Dome, floor and approach","color":"#6a4a34","description":"The vaulted dome, marble floor and altar, and the Vermilion Steps approach."}],"explanations":{"terrace level first":"The lowest marble terrace level; the three tiers rise 6 m in total. Radius is schematic.","terrace level second":"The middle marble terrace level. Radius is schematic.","terrace level third":"The top marble terrace level carrying the hall. Radius is schematic.","balustrades":"The carved white marble balustrades edging the terrace levels. Segmentation is schematic.","terrace stairs":"The south stairs between terrace levels. Width and step counts are schematic.","dragon well pillars":"The four central Dragon Well pillars, 18.5 m high and 1.2 m in diameter, read as the four seasons.","gold pillars north":"Six of the twelve inner gold pillars (the months of the year), north half. Heights are schematic.","gold pillars south":"Six of the twelve inner gold pillars, south half. Heights are schematic.","eave pillars north":"Six of the twelve outer eave pillars (the twelve watches of the day), north half. Heights are schematic.","eave pillars south":"Six of the twelve outer eave pillars, south half. Heights are schematic.","dougong lower ring":"The lower ring of interlocking dougong brackets, no nails, stepping inward layer by layer. Stacking is schematic.","dougong upper ring":"The upper ring of dougong brackets toward the dome. Stacking is schematic.","eave lower":"The lowest blue-tiled eave; the tiles symbolize the sky. Pitch is schematic.","eave middle":"The middle blue-tiled eave. Pitch is schematic.","eave upper":"The upper blue-tiled eave rising to the gilded knob at 38 m. Pitch is schematic.","fascia rings":"The fascia rings edging the three eaves. Profiles are schematic.","drainage spouts":"Schematic rainwater spouts on the lower eave.","gilded baoding":"The gilded baoding knob crowning the roof at 38 m, on its supporting pillar.","vaulted dome":"The vaulted dome carried by the 28 pillars, converging to the apex; the timber frame uses mortise-and-tenon joints, no nails.","marble floor and altar":"The marble floor and central altar platform. Forms are schematic.","vermilion steps approach":"Schematic approach of the 360 m Vermilion Steps Bridge to the Imperial Vault of Heaven. Shown shortened.","wall panels north":"The timber wall panels of the north quadrant. Arrangement is schematic.","wall panels east":"The timber wall panels of the east quadrant. Arrangement is schematic.","wall panels south":"The timber wall panels of the south quadrant. Arrangement is schematic.","wall panels west":"The timber wall panels of the west quadrant. Arrangement is schematic."},"parts":[{"id":"terrace-level-first","name":"Terrace